  "fragments": [
    {
      "id": "05-B",
      "x": 700,
      "y": 400,
      "bodyText": "Entry 067. I understand now why the wanderer's light is mine. I put it there. Not intentionally — not in the way I built the platforms or the portals. I put it there the way a person puts something in a place they forgot they had. The wanderer is not a stranger in my simulation. They are its last memory of what I was before I started to change.",
      "unlock": "NONE"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-A",
      "x": 100,
      "y": 200,
      "bodyText": "Entry 071. The apprentice knows. They figured it out without being told. I watched them choose to keep building platforms even after they understood what the cores are. That choice is either the bravest thing I have seen in this simulation or the most naïve. I have not decided which.",
      "unlock": "NONE"
    }
